1
00:00:12,674 --> 00:00:14,574
Falling leaves again...

2
00:00:15,274 --> 00:00:18,374
It's going to be tough sweeping
tomorrow morning.

3
00:00:18,814 --> 00:00:20,684
Looks like that's going to be tough, too.

4
00:00:30,464 --> 00:00:32,224
Ms. Sayaka.

5
00:00:37,634 --> 00:00:40,154
Isn't there any way that I can be of help?

6
00:00:42,474 --> 00:00:44,064
Oh, Kobato!

7
00:00:44,304 --> 00:00:45,634
Welcome home!

8
00:00:46,004 --> 00:00:47,444
Hello everybody.

9
00:00:47,544 --> 00:00:50,244
Were you all out somewhere this afternoon?

10
00:00:50,644 --> 00:00:55,344
Yes. There was a meeting at their
school for the coming bazaar.

11
00:00:55,754 --> 00:00:56,684
Bazaar?

12
00:00:57,254 --> 00:00:59,154
Everybody brings something.

13
00:00:59,224 --> 00:01:02,084
And we sell it and use
the money for the school.

14
00:01:03,764 --> 00:01:05,024
That's it!

15
00:01:10,604 --> 00:01:13,734
Kobato.

16
00:01:13,734 --> 00:01:16,574
Kobato.
Dou sureba iin dakke?

17
00:01:16,574 --> 00:01:20,974
Kobato.
Atarimae no kototte itsumo

18
00:01:21,874 --> 00:01:25,184
Muzukashii na

19
00:01:25,184 --> 00:01:27,954
Ureshii toki waratte

20
00:01:27,954 --> 00:01:32,254
Suki na toki ni utaitai dake

21
00:01:32,824 --> 00:01:35,254
Na no ni

22
00:01:36,554 --> 00:01:40,924
Itsuka negai wa kanau to

23
00:01:41,364 --> 00:01:44,634
Demo "itsuka" tte dore kurai?

24
00:01:44,634 --> 00:01:48,124
Machikirenai yo

25
00:01:48,274 --> 00:01:54,044
123! no aizu de ryoute hirogete

26
00:01:54,044 --> 00:01:59,244
Zenshin ni hikari wo atsumete

27
00:01:59,244 --> 00:02:02,084
Doko ni aru no?

28
00:02:02,084 --> 00:02:05,424
Oshiete, watashi ni dekiru koto

29
00:02:05,424 --> 00:02:08,254
Meippai kizu tsuite

30
00:02:08,254 --> 00:02:11,164
Seiippai hashitte

31
00:02:11,164 --> 00:02:15,134
Nan juu kai koronde naite

32
00:02:15,134 --> 00:02:18,164
Sore de mo mada

33
00:02:18,164 --> 00:02:22,194
Akireru kurai

34
00:02:22,674 --> 00:02:26,834
Ashita wo shinjiteru

35
00:02:36,684 --> 00:02:42,214
...Mysterious Life Form.

36
00:02:43,254 --> 00:02:44,414
A bazaar!

37
00:02:46,664 --> 00:02:49,064
Ms. Sayaka, let's have a bazaar!

38
00:02:49,064 --> 00:02:49,794
What?

39
00:02:49,794 --> 00:02:53,734
We can sell all kinds of things, lots of it,
and make money to pay off the debt!

40
00:02:54,774 --> 00:02:56,434
Kobato?

41
00:02:57,004 --> 00:02:57,274
Account Book

42
00:02:57,274 --> 00:03:01,344
Account Book
If we pay off the debt, the kindergarten
doesn't have to move out, right?

43
00:03:01,344 --> 00:03:01,704
Account Book

44
00:03:04,744 --> 00:03:07,214
Right? Let's do it! A bazaar!

45
00:03:07,454 --> 00:03:08,684
But Kobato...

46
00:03:08,684 --> 00:03:12,714
If the debt was small enough for a bazaar to
cover, we'd have paid it off ages ago!

47
00:03:13,454 --> 00:03:14,894
Fujimoto?

48
00:03:14,894 --> 00:03:19,854
It's one thing for a big school to have one,
but we're just a tiny kindergarten.

49
00:03:20,134 --> 00:03:21,684
It's not going to be much of a bazaar.

50
00:03:21,864 --> 00:03:24,994
It's just not worth it.

51
00:03:36,214 --> 00:03:40,044
I'm sorry! I got carried away!

52
00:03:40,254 --> 00:03:42,184
I'll go and sweep out front now!

53
00:03:48,854 --> 00:03:55,764
Frankly speaking, if we do a bazaar and it
doesn't work out, it would be hardest on Kobato.

54
00:03:56,764 --> 00:04:00,374
So I understand why you discouraged her.

55
00:04:00,374 --> 00:04:02,664
But that was wrong, the way you said that.

56
00:04:03,874 --> 00:04:07,834
Being overly blunt can make you a mean person.

57
00:04:25,994 --> 00:04:27,394
I...

58
00:04:32,264 --> 00:04:35,134
I got all excited and carried away.

59
00:04:36,604 --> 00:04:41,104
Fujimoto and Ms. Sayaka must
think I'm pretty silly.

60
00:04:42,574 --> 00:04:46,204
I am pretty silly, aren't I?

61
00:04:47,854 --> 00:04:50,014
Yeah, you are pretty silly.

62
00:04:50,754 --> 00:04:54,814
But I see nothing wrong with your enthusiasm.

63
00:04:58,494 --> 00:05:01,014
Ioryogi-san!

64
00:05:01,264 --> 00:05:05,724
Hey! Don't hug me! That's annoying!

65
00:05:07,234 --> 00:05:08,704
Kobato?

66
00:05:14,674 --> 00:05:16,264
Ms. Sayaka?

67
00:05:17,684 --> 00:05:19,544
Let's do it. A bazaar.

68
00:05:20,354 --> 00:05:21,684
Huh?

69
00:05:22,014 --> 00:05:23,414
Bazaar?

70
00:05:24,054 --> 00:05:27,584
We'll all bring things from home
that we no longer need,

71
00:05:27,754 --> 00:05:29,794
or things we made and sell them
here at the kindergarten.

72
00:05:29,794 --> 00:05:31,424
We can play store!

73
00:05:31,424 --> 00:05:33,524
I want to have a fried noodle shop!

74
00:05:34,434 --> 00:05:35,794
That sounds good, too.

75
00:05:36,464 --> 00:05:40,834
I've written the details in your agendas
so be sure to show someone at home.

76
00:05:40,934 --> 00:05:42,134
Okay!

77
00:05:42,134 --> 00:05:43,434
Let's go for it!

78
00:05:43,644 --> 00:05:44,244
Yeah!

79
00:05:44,244 --> 00:05:45,434
Fujimoto.
Yeah!

80
00:05:47,044 --> 00:05:49,804
Kobato seems to be feeling much
better now. Isn't that wonderful?

81
00:05:50,414 --> 00:05:52,144
It's none of my business.

82
00:05:55,714 --> 00:05:56,754
Bye-bye!

83
00:05:56,754 --> 00:05:58,944
Ms. Sayaka, see you tomorrow!

84
00:05:59,054 --> 00:06:00,454
Yes, goodbye!

85
00:06:03,094 --> 00:06:03,454
Bazaar...

86
00:06:03,454 --> 00:06:04,964
(Yomogi) Kindergarten
Bazaar
Bazaar...

87
00:06:04,964 --> 00:06:06,894
(Yomogi) Kindergarten
Bazaar

88
00:06:09,494 --> 00:06:10,704
What's this?

89
00:06:10,704 --> 00:06:11,964
It's a puppy!

90
00:06:12,104 --> 00:06:12,964
And that one?

91
00:06:12,964 --> 00:06:14,454
A kitty!

92
00:06:17,204 --> 00:06:19,804
Don't you think you're being
unkind to cats and dogs?

93
00:06:23,714 --> 00:06:26,344
What can she say? He's telling the truth.

94
00:06:28,684 --> 00:06:29,984
Have some tea.

95
00:06:32,124 --> 00:06:33,814
Thank you very much.

96
00:06:35,124 --> 00:06:36,994
Did you draw this, Kobato?

97
00:06:36,994 --> 00:06:38,224
Yes!

98
00:06:38,664 --> 00:06:39,784
It's very good.

99
00:06:43,064 --> 00:06:46,264
Really. That's a really cute duck and sheep!

100
00:06:49,904 --> 00:06:51,964
Well then, I've got to go now.

101
00:06:52,804 --> 00:06:53,944
Are you working?

102
00:06:53,944 --> 00:06:55,104
Yes.

103
00:06:56,044 --> 00:06:57,444
Don't push yourself.

104
00:06:58,614 --> 00:07:01,674
I'm not. Ms. Sayaka, you too.

105
00:07:03,014 --> 00:07:04,414
Please take it easy.

106
00:07:08,454 --> 00:07:12,514
So that's how Fujimoto smiles.

107
00:07:19,864 --> 00:07:23,534
Mysterious Life Form

108
00:07:24,244 --> 00:07:26,004
Goodbye.

109
00:07:28,514 --> 00:07:30,704
He behaves like a little boy sometimes.

110
00:07:31,384 --> 00:07:34,054
I think he likes you, Kobato.

111
00:07:34,054 --> 00:07:35,384
What?!

112
00:07:35,384 --> 00:07:36,684
Really.

113
00:07:36,984 --> 00:07:40,644
He's not very good at showing his
honest feelings. Just like that man.

114
00:07:41,754 --> 00:07:42,984
That man?

115
00:07:44,424 --> 00:07:46,584
Kobato! Thank you for all of your help today.

116
00:07:47,664 --> 00:07:50,684
Let's continue bazaar preparations tomorrow.

117
00:07:59,404 --> 00:08:01,004
When she said, "that man..."

118
00:08:02,044 --> 00:08:04,744
Could she have been talking
about her husband?

119
00:08:06,244 --> 00:08:11,414
You once ordered a birthday cake
for your husband, didn't you?

120
00:08:11,824 --> 00:08:13,754
Uh... yes...

121
00:08:17,124 --> 00:08:18,264
Could be.

122
00:08:18,264 --> 00:08:22,754
She said he's not good at showing his honest
feelings. I wonder what he's like.

123
00:08:23,394 --> 00:08:24,694
Beats me.

124
00:08:24,764 --> 00:08:26,034
It's a mystery.

125
00:08:26,034 --> 00:08:28,434
Not as much of a mystery as
your drawings, Dobato!

126
00:08:30,034 --> 00:08:32,234
You're mean!

127
00:08:34,514 --> 00:08:36,504
Wow!

128
00:08:36,974 --> 00:08:39,474
Thank you, everyone!

129
00:08:44,024 --> 00:08:45,454
What's this?

130
00:08:45,454 --> 00:08:47,084
Teru teru bozu dolls!

131
00:08:47,194 --> 00:08:48,654
Teru teru bozu?

132
00:08:48,654 --> 00:08:52,284
Um, they're weather dolls. You hang
them up to make it sunny outside.

133
00:08:52,464 --> 00:08:54,454
I wonder who brought them.

134
00:08:56,464 --> 00:08:58,364
Naomi, did you make these?

135
00:08:59,264 --> 00:09:00,534
Mhm.

136
00:09:01,004 --> 00:09:03,534
The weather's usually good when
I make the teru teru bozu dolls.

137
00:09:03,534 --> 00:09:08,944
The day of the picnic... and when we
went to the pool, it became sunny.

138
00:09:09,314 --> 00:09:12,144
Pretty amazing weather dolls, aren't they?

139
00:09:12,944 --> 00:09:14,544
I wonder if they'll sell.

140
00:09:14,954 --> 00:09:18,484
Sure! I'll make something too.

141
00:09:18,484 --> 00:09:20,354
Let's line them up for sale together.

142
00:09:20,524 --> 00:09:21,754
Let's!

143
00:09:21,994 --> 00:09:26,014
So. Let's start putting price tags on
the things you all brought.

144
00:09:26,524 --> 00:09:27,294
Okay, write them nice and big here.

145
00:09:27,294 --> 00:09:28,594
Kobato...
Okay, write them nice and big here.

146
00:09:28,594 --> 00:09:29,254
Okay, write them nice and big here.

147
00:09:32,364 --> 00:09:33,594
Yes Naomi?

148
00:09:33,804 --> 00:09:38,404
If a lot of people buy weather dolls,
can the kindergarten stay?

149
00:09:38,404 --> 00:09:40,204
Yes, It sure can.

150
00:09:40,544 --> 00:09:43,204
Um, well... my mommy's going to...

151
00:09:44,384 --> 00:09:47,474
My mommy's going to have a baby soon.

152
00:09:47,854 --> 00:09:51,084
That's wonderful! Congratulations!

153
00:09:51,254 --> 00:09:52,444
So you see...

154
00:09:53,354 --> 00:09:57,584
Mommy is taking time off
work starting this month,

155
00:09:57,994 --> 00:10:01,894
but when the baby gets bigger,
she's going to work again.

156
00:10:02,394 --> 00:10:06,024
She wants to have the baby come
to Yomogi Kindergarten.

157
00:10:06,434 --> 00:10:10,664
And because I'm going to be the big sister,
I'll come to pick her up!

158
00:10:11,544 --> 00:10:15,174
Then I'll still be able to see you
and Ms. Sayaka every day!

159
00:10:15,544 --> 00:10:19,744
I want to see you when you're a big sister, too!

160
00:10:20,284 --> 00:10:22,614
Everybody, let's make this happen!

161
00:10:22,614 --> 00:10:24,324
Yes!

162
00:10:24,324 --> 00:10:24,554
Yomogi Kindergarten
Bazaar
Yes!

163
00:10:24,554 --> 00:10:29,324
Yomogi Kindergarten
Bazaar

164
00:10:59,154 --> 00:11:01,644
Oh, we worked very late.

165
00:11:01,854 --> 00:11:03,354
Are you with Yomogi Kindergarten?

166
00:11:03,354 --> 00:11:04,464
Huh?

167
00:11:04,464 --> 00:11:06,154
Ah, yes!

168
00:11:07,294 --> 00:11:11,024
I recognize your voice.
I talked to you on the phone.

169
00:11:12,534 --> 00:11:14,734
And you are?

170
00:11:21,744 --> 00:11:23,504
I'm a debt collector.

171
00:11:42,364 --> 00:11:44,194
I'm shutting down the kindergarten.

172
00:11:45,234 --> 00:11:47,494
I'm not extending the repayment deadline.

173
00:11:49,774 --> 00:11:51,704
That phone call...

174
00:11:54,044 --> 00:11:55,144
Working overtime?

175
00:11:55,144 --> 00:11:59,744
No! We were putting up posters
for the bazaar and we...!

176
00:12:00,784 --> 00:12:03,874
You are a bad man so I tell you nothing!

177
00:12:04,284 --> 00:12:08,274
You're quite a character. I also thought
so when we talked over the phone.

178
00:12:11,194 --> 00:12:13,124
Did you give my message to Sayaka?

179
00:12:14,464 --> 00:12:16,794
That's she's not getting an extension?

180
00:12:18,864 --> 00:12:22,594
Tell her also that you saw me here today.

181
00:12:23,434 --> 00:12:27,504
And that when the due date arrives,
I'm going to shut down the kindergarten.

182
00:12:27,674 --> 00:12:28,874
You can't do that!

183
00:12:29,144 --> 00:12:31,044
I don't care if children are attending.

184
00:12:31,814 --> 00:12:35,404
Tell her if she doesn't want anyone injured,
to pack her things and go.

185
00:12:41,224 --> 00:12:42,984
See you around, Kobato.

186
00:12:56,734 --> 00:13:00,234
Do you think he's serious...
about shutting down the kindergarten?

187
00:13:05,344 --> 00:13:08,004
Even if children are attending... that's terrible.

188
00:13:08,614 --> 00:13:12,784
How can he look so kind and
say such awful things?

189
00:13:12,784 --> 00:13:14,324
That man scares me.

190
00:13:14,324 --> 00:13:16,294
What kind of a man?

191
00:13:16,554 --> 00:13:19,584
F-Fujimoto! Were you listening?

192
00:13:19,894 --> 00:13:23,294
I overheard you talking to yourself
in that big voice of yours!

193
00:13:23,394 --> 00:13:24,764
I wasn't talking to myself...

194
00:13:27,974 --> 00:13:29,464
What was he like?

195
00:13:30,804 --> 00:13:32,964
H-He didn't give me his name.

196
00:13:33,274 --> 00:13:35,574
He just smiled a lot.

197
00:13:36,644 --> 00:13:40,774
Oh, and he was calling
Ms. Sayaka just "Sayaka."

198
00:13:40,984 --> 00:13:42,284
Okiura...

199
00:13:42,684 --> 00:13:43,744
Huh?

200
00:13:46,754 --> 00:13:48,224
Someone you know?

201
00:13:48,324 --> 00:13:51,364
Did Ms. Sayaka meet him?

202
00:13:51,364 --> 00:13:56,994
N-No... After he talked to me, he just left.

203
00:13:58,264 --> 00:13:59,594
Don't say a word to her.

204
00:14:00,704 --> 00:14:02,724
Don't tell Ms. Sayaka that you saw him.

205
00:14:03,834 --> 00:14:04,804
But!

206
00:14:05,344 --> 00:14:07,004
Just keep your mouth shut about it.

207
00:14:16,254 --> 00:14:21,214
Why did you go there? You make more trouble
for Ms. Sayaka and I won't stand for it.

208
00:14:21,924 --> 00:14:26,364
Now you listen to me. Don't be showing
your face at her place either.

209
00:14:28,794 --> 00:14:30,534
That man...

210
00:14:30,534 --> 00:14:31,624
Huh?

211
00:14:32,604 --> 00:14:38,934
His name is Okiura, isn't it? I wonder
what his connection to Ms. Sayaka is.

212
00:14:39,104 --> 00:14:40,744
Why that's totally obvious!

213
00:14:40,744 --> 00:14:41,774
Huh?

214
00:14:41,774 --> 00:14:46,614
That woman Sayaka was apparently married
and her last name is the same as that man's.

215
00:14:46,814 --> 00:14:49,344
And he calls her Sayaka!

216
00:14:51,624 --> 00:14:57,184
WHAT?! Then that man is
Ms. Sayaka's husband?!

217
00:14:58,024 --> 00:15:01,824
Why would he want to put
the kindergarten under?

218
00:15:06,504 --> 00:15:09,474
Don't you get yourself too involved in this case.

219
00:15:09,874 --> 00:15:11,034
Huh?

220
00:15:11,304 --> 00:15:13,794
Besides, don't you have things to do?

221
00:15:14,814 --> 00:15:18,944
You won't be able to go where you want to go
until that bottle is full, you know that?

222
00:15:22,884 --> 00:15:25,714
But... I'm worried...

223
00:15:35,064 --> 00:15:38,364
And? What is that you're sewing?

224
00:15:38,464 --> 00:15:40,034
It's a mascot!

225
00:15:40,034 --> 00:15:42,524
I'm making it from cloth Ms. Chitose gave me!

226
00:15:46,704 --> 00:15:47,834
Is it a penguin?

227
00:15:49,774 --> 00:15:51,714
It's a rabbit.

228
00:15:54,284 --> 00:15:56,184
Those are ears?!

229
00:15:56,714 --> 00:15:59,954
Call it what you like! Okay, it's a penguin then!

230
00:16:00,184 --> 00:16:03,924
Anyway, I am going to do my best to
see that the bazaar is a success!

231
00:16:03,994 --> 00:16:07,524
Then, you plan to mass-produce
that mysterious life form?!

232
00:16:07,524 --> 00:16:11,334
Hey, you're beginning to sound like Fujimoto!

233
00:16:11,334 --> 00:16:13,494
You are mean!

234
00:16:14,404 --> 00:16:18,564
Yomogi Kindergarten
Bazaar Hall

235
00:16:21,214 --> 00:16:23,234
Looks like heavy clouds today.

236
00:16:23,914 --> 00:16:25,034
It'll be all right!

237
00:16:26,044 --> 00:16:28,144
The clouds will clear, I'm sure.

238
00:16:28,584 --> 00:16:30,014
I certainly hope so.

239
00:16:34,224 --> 00:16:35,394
Ioryogi-san?

240
00:16:35,394 --> 00:16:38,514
I'll bring you something that will surely sell.

241
00:16:40,094 --> 00:16:41,754
Thank you very much!

242
00:16:43,164 --> 00:16:46,064
Let's all give it our best today!

243
00:16:46,064 --> 00:16:48,094
Yes!

244
00:16:51,874 --> 00:16:55,134
I'm sure the weather dolls will
turn it into nice weather.

245
00:16:56,414 --> 00:16:57,474
Yeah!

246
00:16:58,344 --> 00:16:59,614
Kobato.

247
00:16:59,614 --> 00:17:00,984
Don't fall down, okay?

248
00:17:00,984 --> 00:17:02,854
We're going to be selling drinks and stuff too.

249
00:17:02,854 --> 00:17:04,254
I-I will not fall down.

250
00:17:04,254 --> 00:17:04,884
You'll fall down.

251
00:17:04,884 --> 00:17:05,654
Huh!

252
00:17:05,654 --> 00:17:07,674
I will not! I refuse to fall down!

253
00:17:08,154 --> 00:17:10,684
You two really get along well.

254
00:17:11,024 --> 00:17:12,354
We do not get along.

255
00:17:12,494 --> 00:17:13,654
We don't!

256
00:17:16,464 --> 00:17:20,764
Oh this. Fujimoto had this donated from work.

257
00:17:30,544 --> 00:17:32,274
Thank you very much.

258
00:17:32,784 --> 00:17:34,974
What did I tell you? You fell.

259
00:17:35,754 --> 00:17:37,244
I'm sorry.

260
00:17:39,024 --> 00:17:40,784
Don't get your hopes up too high.

261
00:17:40,784 --> 00:17:42,184
Huh?

262
00:17:51,264 --> 00:17:52,894
Oh no, I've got to go!

263
00:17:55,774 --> 00:17:57,934
Kobato, You fell down after all.

264
00:18:17,764 --> 00:18:19,794
We aren't getting any customers.

265
00:18:19,794 --> 00:18:22,054
We put all those posters up together.

266
00:18:23,034 --> 00:18:24,264
Don't worry.

267
00:18:24,364 --> 00:18:26,964
Your mothers probably won't be
here until much later,

268
00:18:27,134 --> 00:18:29,834
but other customers will be
showing up soon, I'm sure.

269
00:18:30,604 --> 00:18:31,904
Really?

270
00:18:38,144 --> 00:18:41,014
What if nobody comes?

271
00:18:51,594 --> 00:18:55,124
It's all because I suggested having a bazaar.

272
00:19:01,534 --> 00:19:02,734
Hello.

273
00:19:04,804 --> 00:19:06,204
Chitose!

274
00:19:07,444 --> 00:19:09,874
Kobato told us and we've been
looking forward to it.

275
00:19:09,874 --> 00:19:10,344
Weren't we?

276
00:19:10,344 --> 00:19:10,874
Right?
Weren't we?

277
00:19:10,874 --> 00:19:11,704
Right?
Right!

278
00:19:13,284 --> 00:19:14,984
Would you like some fried noodles?

279
00:19:14,984 --> 00:19:16,654
We've got iced coffee, too.

280
00:19:16,654 --> 00:19:18,484
Or café au lait if you like.

281
00:19:19,324 --> 00:19:21,554
Thank you for coming.

282
00:19:21,554 --> 00:19:26,084
We were really looking forward to it.
Chiho and Chise, too. But...

283
00:19:26,994 --> 00:19:32,304
When we looked today, the posters were gone
so we were worried that it had been canceled.

284
00:19:32,304 --> 00:19:33,464
What?

285
00:19:34,704 --> 00:19:36,224
Oh, no...

286
00:19:36,434 --> 00:19:38,804
Don't tell me that guy's responsible for this.

287
00:19:41,344 --> 00:19:42,574
Kobato?!

288
00:19:42,574 --> 00:19:46,074
I'm going to tell everybody that the
bazaar has not been canceled!

289
00:19:47,814 --> 00:19:49,654
Isn't it kind of late for that?!

290
00:19:49,654 --> 00:19:53,084
It's not too late! People still may come!

291
00:19:53,084 --> 00:19:56,214
But still, this is just a tiny little bazaar.

292
00:19:56,394 --> 00:20:00,454
Even so, it would be worth it if I can get even
one more person to come! Because...

293
00:20:00,624 --> 00:20:03,754
Because we all, all the children
worked very hard on this!

294
00:20:04,264 --> 00:20:06,204
All of us... together...

295
00:20:06,604 --> 00:20:07,934
Kobato...

296
00:20:08,004 --> 00:20:09,934
Fujimoto, you too! Didn't you?!

297
00:20:21,854 --> 00:20:24,084
Kobato's a good kid.

298
00:20:24,954 --> 00:20:26,424
She really is.

299
00:20:29,094 --> 00:20:30,554
Fujimoto?

300
00:20:31,394 --> 00:20:34,984
Well she says she's going to get people to come,
I'd better get some coffee ready.

301
00:20:35,764 --> 00:20:37,954
A bit twisted, but he's a good kid too.

302
00:20:38,764 --> 00:20:40,134
Yes.

303
00:20:45,404 --> 00:20:46,844
A chicken?

304
00:20:47,004 --> 00:20:48,404
A seal?

305
00:20:50,444 --> 00:20:52,204
Still nobody.

306
00:20:52,314 --> 00:20:54,084
Although it's stopped raining.

307
00:20:54,084 --> 00:20:55,914
Even the sun's coming out.

308
00:20:58,224 --> 00:20:59,844
Good afternoon.

309
00:21:01,054 --> 00:21:03,684
Is this where the Bazaar is?

310
00:21:04,994 --> 00:21:06,324
Yes.

311
00:21:06,664 --> 00:21:11,824
Kobato came to tell me about it and
I thought I'd come for a look.

312
00:21:13,164 --> 00:21:14,764
Hey, this is it here!

313
00:21:15,604 --> 00:21:17,334
I heard you're having a bazaar.

314
00:21:17,434 --> 00:21:19,874
Oh, perhaps I can find a bargain.

315
00:21:20,004 --> 00:21:21,034
This looks like fun.

316
00:21:21,514 --> 00:21:22,674
Where do you want to go first?

317
00:21:22,874 --> 00:21:24,144
Welcome!

318
00:21:35,094 --> 00:21:36,114
Looks busy.

319
00:21:36,594 --> 00:21:37,714
Domoto...

320
00:21:38,094 --> 00:21:40,154
Yeah, Kobato told me.

321
00:21:40,824 --> 00:21:43,294
Hasn't she come back yet?

322
00:21:45,734 --> 00:21:47,264
Can I get an iced coffee?

323
00:21:47,264 --> 00:21:50,634
Ah, yes! Teacher Fujimoto,
one iced coffee please!

324
00:21:51,274 --> 00:21:52,504
Here you are.

325
00:21:52,904 --> 00:21:56,114
Hey. There was this young lady,
she's walking the streets shouting,

326
00:21:56,114 --> 00:22:00,984
"Bazaar at Yomogi Kindergarten," you know...

327
00:22:01,714 --> 00:22:01,884
Bazaar everybody!

328
00:22:01,884 --> 00:22:04,214
Like she was putting everything she had into it.
Bazaar everybody!

329
00:22:04,414 --> 00:22:07,454
So well I said, "Hey, I'll check it out later,"

330
00:22:07,454 --> 00:22:11,024
and she grabbed my hand and
started shaking it like mad.

331
00:22:11,024 --> 00:22:13,324
Thank you very much!

332
00:22:13,824 --> 00:22:15,424
I can just see it.

333
00:22:16,064 --> 00:22:17,424
Sounds just like her.

334
00:22:21,434 --> 00:22:22,234
Mommy!

335
00:22:22,234 --> 00:22:24,864
Naomi, I'm sorry I'm late.

336
00:22:25,174 --> 00:22:27,764
Look at all the customers you have.

337
00:22:27,904 --> 00:22:29,204
Yeah.

338
00:22:30,844 --> 00:22:33,674
Good thing the weather cleared up.

339
00:22:38,354 --> 00:22:39,684
Mhm!

340
00:22:43,354 --> 00:22:46,484
Bazaar today at Yomogi Kindergarten!

341
00:22:48,064 --> 00:22:51,224
Everybody, please come and check it out!

342
00:22:52,504 --> 00:22:55,604
Yomogi Kindergarten Bazaar!

343
00:22:55,604 --> 00:22:58,094
It's happening right now!

344
00:23:01,374 --> 00:23:09,014
Hito wa mina tonde mitai no ni

345
00:23:10,184 --> 00:23:16,284
Juuryoku ni damasareterunda

346
00:23:16,554 --> 00:23:24,394
Dare mo honto wa toberunda yo

347
00:23:26,634 --> 00:23:32,974
Ano ko ga anna ni kanashisou na no wa

348
00:23:34,004 --> 00:23:36,874
Jibun no kage wo

349
00:23:36,874 --> 00:23:44,014
Dokoka ni wasurete kichatta kara kamo

350
00:23:44,184 --> 00:23:46,714
Sore nara

351
00:23:46,884 --> 00:23:50,994
"Arigatou," tte kimi ni ietara

352
00:23:50,994 --> 00:23:54,864
"Arigatou," tte kimi ga waraeba

353
00:23:54,864 --> 00:24:02,204
Ittari kitari ureshiku naru

354
00:24:02,734 --> 00:24:06,974
Kimi ga shiawase ni naru

355
00:24:07,274 --> 00:24:11,514
Shinpai nante iranai yo

356
00:24:11,514 --> 00:24:15,604
Issho ni iru kara

357
00:24:17,384 --> 00:24:23,324
Ureshikuttemo namida ga deru nante

358
00:24:23,324 --> 00:24:26,064
Fushigi da

359
00:24:26,064 --> 00:24:29,064
Next episode
...Mysterious Life Form II.
Fushigi da

360
